WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.680
Now do the Full Turn Extension.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.970
1, 2, down, up!

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.020
Do it again!

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.560
Right. I'm sorry.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.810
Thank you very much!

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.270
Hm?

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:35.180
What's wrong?

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.430
N-Nothing!

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:37.810
Nothing at all!

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.310
Guys, you're being rude to our coach.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.770
We're sorry!

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.680
Kirari, Kirari...

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.850
You've already read my message,
so why won't you reply?

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:48.600
Kirari?

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.470
Hey, don't invade my privacy!

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:53.430
You're the one talking to yourself.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.310
Gen, do you know anythin'?

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:56.640
Notta thing!

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.930
Hey, wait a sec, you do know!

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:04.350
What's going on? Gin, Doh, and now
Ichiro have all been acting strange.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.430
Kazu...

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:08.470
Kazu?

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.180
Oh, sorry!

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.520
What is it?

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:36.430
<i>I'll put an end to spending</i>
<i>my days so thoughtlessly</i>

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:40.470
<i>I'm dying to break free of this</i>

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:46.220
<i>Since I can never take that first step forward,</i>

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:50.310
<i>you always take my hand and pull me along</i>

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:56.140
<i>You've brought me to see</i>
<i>something completely new</i>

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.430
<i>My whole world is changing</i>

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:01.640
<i>With that first step</i>

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.810
<i>I felt transformed</i>

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:09.770
<i>I can go anywhere; it'll work</i>
<i>out so long as we're together</i>

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.350
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:12.970
<i>just as you are</i>

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:16.140
<i>At times you'll feel lost and scared,</i>

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:22.640
<i>but there are so many things you</i>
<i>won't know if you never give them a go</i>

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.270
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:29.180
<i>stretch out your hands until</i>
<i>you're almost touching the sky</i>

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.430
<i>We're not alone anymore</i>

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:37.560
<i>Together we'll fly into a new world</i>

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.020
Men's Locker Room

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.220
Kazu, is something wrong?

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.770
No, nothing's wrong.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:55.560
But...

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.640
I was just thinking a bit.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:03.680
That since we've raised the bar for the qualifiers,
practice is gonna be tough from here on out.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:06.390
It's troubling to hear our
Captain sound so pessimistic.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.520
You're right. Sorry!

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:15.560
It's easy to turn over some broccoli, but turning
someone around 360 degrees is super hard.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.520
That's right, bro.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:18.680
Bro?

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.930
Takumi, stop calling everyone that.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.470
Got it, Bro.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:27.350
Hey, Sho. Is there a trick to
the Full Turn Extension, bro?

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.640
You just don't get it!

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:35.600
A trick? When lifting up the flyer, use their
heel as an axis, then turn their toes around.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.600
That's when you make the twist.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.890
Say that again?

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:41.350
I'd like to know, too!

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:47.270
Kazu, I'm sorry. I couldn't
do it at all. How can I turn...

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:47.930
Kazu?

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:50.220
Huh? Oh, sorry!

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:52.430
I'm in a bit of a rush.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:01.850
I knew Kazu was acting strangely.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.350
Sis.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.270
Uh, hey.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:21.350
Are you okay?

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:22.970
What do you mean, am I okay?

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:26.020
No, I just, somehow...

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.520
Shouldn't I be asking you that?

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.390
I saw you at the school festival.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:37.640
Doing that stuff with a bunch of guys. And you've
brought a ton of things up onto the roof, haven't you?

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:39.720
What are you doing?

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.600
Just what in the world are you doing?

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.720
I-I'm sorry.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.310
What? Kazu's taking today off?

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:06.180
Yes. He let me know.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.310
I hadn't heard.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:09.770
Haru, did you hear anything?

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.640
No.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.600
What could he be up to
with the qualifiers so close?

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:19.430
Yes, this will make practicing the
new stunts we added more difficult.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.930
A man always looks straight ahead.

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:24.350
Y-Yessir!

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:26.310
Look people in the eyes when you answer them.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.970
Y-Yessir!

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:32.770
Well, anyway, we should get started!
Let's buckle down and finish early today!

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.680
Gen, did sumthin' good happen?

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.430
No, nuthin' special.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.100
Our teammates seem restless for some reason.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.520
They do.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:45.310
And that reason is...

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:46.470
That reason is...?

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.270
Love!

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:49.680
I get it!

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:50.430
You see?

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.770
You've probably never even been in love.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.020
Seems like it might be love.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.220
Huh?

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.270
W-Who?

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:05.220
Kirari!

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.560
Like I said, who?!

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:07.970
My kid sister.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.350
You have a little sister?

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.390
She's mega cute!

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:15.810
If she's that cute, then how about
keeping a brotherly eye on her?

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:19.770
I wonder if I can! Thing is,
I think she has a date today.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.810
How do you know something like that?

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:26.470
I was worried, so I ended up secretly
listenin' to her on the phone!

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:31.600
She won't even tell me who it is.
She caught me eavesdroppin',

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.890
so she's been ignorin' all my messages lately.

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:37.600
That's why I need you to help me!

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:38.810
Huh?

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.850
They should be meetin' here.

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:46.060
Why're we staking out your sister's date spot?

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:51.100
First we'll size up her date, and if
he's creepy, I'll beat the hell outta him.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:54.930
Won't that just make her give you
more of the silent treatment?

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.850
You don't have a little sister,
so you wouldn't understand.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:02.930
If that's how you feel, then why
didn't you ask Gen? Or maybe Kazu?

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:07.640
Gen's been actin' weird
lately, too. He's avoidin' me.

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:08.930
Kazu seems funny, too.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:09.680
Huh?

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:10.770
Maybe they're both...

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:12.970
I-In love?!

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:18.720
N-Not Kazu. If he found a girl,
he'd definitely tell me.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.350
Isn't she cute?

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:23.220
Y-Yeah...

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:28.060
Well... in an unexpectedly cute kind of way?

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:28.970
That so?

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:32.560
Gen was certainly in high spirits today...

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.220
Is he on a date, too?

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:43.220
Gen, did I make you wait?

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:43.890
It's Kirari!

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:44.850
What?!

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:47.520
Hey, Kirari, I just got here.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:49.220
I'm glad!

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:52.140
Wait, so it's... Gen?

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:54.720
He's been hittin' on my sister?

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:56.060
Wait a minute!

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:00.310
Your outfit today is so cute!
It really suits ya.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:08.600
Where're we goin'? I'll take you anywhere
you want. I'm your knight for the day.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:10.470
Who's a knight, now?!

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:11.600
Ichiro!

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.350
Big Brother?

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.890
Ichiro?

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:29.970
Kirari picked out this present for me!

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:36.390
She said she didn't know what to get for
your birthday, so I promised to help her out.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:38.600
Thank goodness it was just a misunderstanding.

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:41.680
Little sisters. The never-ending romance.

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.310
A misunderstanding?

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:45.470
Maybe we've done the same thing.

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:46.520
Huh?

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.470
You see, Coach Takagi sent us this.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:52.100
Everybody focus!

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:55.890
Your cradle is loose!

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.680
What's with this Sho fan video?

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.680
You're right, it's nothing but him.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:07.600
That's the point! We think
she sent it to us by mistake.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:11.470
Could this mean that the coach l-likes him?

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:12.520
Seriously?!

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.810
Whoa! I think older ladies are A-OK!

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:18.310
We can't bring ourselves to tell Kin.

00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:21.180
But we feel so bad about hiding it.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:22.560
It's hell!

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.640
Haru, you gotta do something!

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:31.390
Eh? The video I sent to Gin?

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:36.350
Oh, I'm so sorry, that was my mistake.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:40.970
I'm sending that specifically
to one of Sho's fans.

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:42.390
A fan?

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.350
Keep it a secret from him for now.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.350
I'll explain everything another time.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.350
All right.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:51.140
So it was all a misunderstanding?

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:52.850
That's great!

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:57.140
You were just quick to
make assumptions about it.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:09:58.390
And probably about Kazu, too.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:01.680
Right, we're starting practice!

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.470
Huh? Where's Kazu?

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:05.930
He's not here again.

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:08.600
He didn't contact me, either.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:10.520
Not a word?

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:13.930
Have you heard anything, Haru?

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:15.520
No...

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:18.260
<b>Caf</b>

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:18.260
<b>Sunflower</b>

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:20.270
Kazu never even showed up.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.350
He's not reading his messages, either.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.470
This is just too strange.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.560
I wonder if something happened.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:32.680
Back when we did judo, Kazu never
missed practice without notice.

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:36.890
This is an unprecedented event.
It has to be love.

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:38.560
I think I get it.

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:40.100
Do you?

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.810
I know how he feels.

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:43.060
Big Bro!

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:44.770
Is he on a date with a girl?

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:47.770
Maybe it isn't going well.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:50.770
You mean the shock of getting
dumped made him miss practice?

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:52.640
She broke his heart?

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:55.890
Kazu would never miss practice
over something like that.

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:59.350
Hey, let's not jump to conclusions here.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.890
I'll go check out Kazu's place.

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:13.020
Yes, please do.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.310
Haru.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:18.270
Um, Kazu could be at the hospital.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:19.220
Huh?

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:23.020
I was worried, so I followed after him.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:27.350
Maybe his grandma isn't feeling well...

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:32.850
She was doing great! No matter how many apples
I peeled, she ate so many that I couldn't keep up.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:36.850
Man, when I'm there she talks
non-stop and won't let me leave!

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:41.310
Got it. I'll try going to the hospital.

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:44.520
Kohinata Hospital

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:03.060
Haru.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:12.220
Thank you.

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:19.560
Sorry about practice.

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.770
Uh-huh.

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:26.390
The coach told me earlier that
a team's captain is its sun.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:30.930
I can't shine brightly as I am now, so...

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:34.270
Everyone's making a big fuss about
how you probably got a girlfriend

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:37.850
and might've been dumped by her.

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:41.390
What the hell, guys.

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:44.640
Is your grandma not doing well?

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:49.350
I've been lying to you this whole time.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:54.680
About her eating lots of apples, and talking
so much that she wouldn't let me leave...

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:59.180
I wish all that was true, but, Granny...

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:03.020
She doesn't know who I am anymore.

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:11.390
She's slowly losing her memories.
There's so many things she can no longer recall.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:15.640
But when she saw some cheerleaders on TV...

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.350
Kasu...

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:24.310
Kasumi...

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:31.350
"Kasumi." She said Mom's name.

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:36.060
Even though those cheerleaders
looked nothing like her.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:42.970
That's when I got an idea. If I did Mom's routine,
maybe she would remember me, too.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:50.640
I want us to do this same routine
at the school festival!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:54.180
Haru, I thought about telling you so many times.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:14:04.020
But if I said this is why I do cheerleading, then what
would I do if I lost that motivation? It scared me.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.770
Kazu...

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:11.640
But it's all over. I've lost
the will to do cheerleading.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:17.810
I'm sorry. For selfish reasons I said I wanted
to start something new with you...

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:22.890
That your cheering had an incredible power...
and I even got everyone else involved.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:29.890
Haru, I'm all alone now.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:33.850
My entire family...
The people who looked after me...

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.520
They're gone.

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.430
Kazu.

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:40.140
Look at me.

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:49.390
Kazu, you're not alone. You're not
as isolated as you think you are.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:52.470
Even if your grandma was the reason
why you started cheerleading,

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:55.890
our members have all rallied around you.

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:03.560
Everyone is looking out for you.
You are our sun, after all! You're amazing!

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:05.180
So...

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:06.970
Don't cry!

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:11.100
Don't cry...

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:20.310
Haru, even you're crying...

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:40.020
Welcome home!

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:41.180
I'm back.

00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:42.430
You're late today.

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:43.470
Yeah.

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:45.390
Are you eating dinner?

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:46.350
Yeah.

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:49.770
That reminds me, Kazuma
hasn't been by lately, has he?

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:54.390
Is he busy? He always came for dinner...

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:05.560
I've never seen Kazu look like that before.

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:14.470
I wonder if he's actually been dealing
with this by himself all along...

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.520
So that's what happened...

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:23.930
Yeah.

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:28.470
I never got why Kazu always tried
to act so bright and cheery.

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:31.640
Yeah... We didn't notice at all.

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:34.430
He made sure we wouldn't.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:40.890
What's with him?! We're a team. Not being able to say
you're hurtin' when times are tough just isn't right!

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:43.970
Cheerleading is the ultimate team sport, after all!

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:48.390
I'm sure being around all of you
really made him happy.

00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:50.930
I know how he feels.

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:55.850
So he insisted on recruiting seven people at first
because he wanted to show his grandmother.

00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:58.770
And that's why he wanted to do
the same routine as his mother...

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:03.770
I get it, so that's what the routine we watched
at the school festival meant to him.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:05.390
Kazu...

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:09.930
I want to support Kazu.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:15.930
I want all of us to support him!

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:16.970
Yeah, so do I!

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:18.220
We shall!

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:22.640
I want to as well. Nothing is
more important than family.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:28.560
I was quite the show-off during my middle and
high school years, and caused my family a lot of trouble.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:33.100
It's a sad story, but now I've
finally come to understand...

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:35.390
...just how important family is.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:36.720
Big Bro...

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:42.810
"Company in distress makes sorrow less."

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:45.220
Dixit William Shakespeare.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:48.270
But how do we support him?

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:50.680
The one thing we can do is...

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.310
...cheer him on.

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.220
Granny, do you want some tea?

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:01.060
Kazuma, how about we open the window?

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:02.600
And the curtains, too.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:08.140
Who are those boys?

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:25.180
A little look won't hurt.

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:28.430
Go on, show your grandmother.

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:34.060
What's going on? What are they doing?

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:41.680
H-Hello everyone! We are the Breakers,
an all-men's cheerleading team!

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:44.350
We hope you enjoy our performance!

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:46.640
Please enjoy our performance!

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:53.140
Go, fight, win! Let's go, Breakers!

00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:55.470
Begin!

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.930
Let's go! Go!

00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:16.770
Meishiin! Hey! C'mon!

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:18.390
We are the Breakers!

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:20.100
This is showtime!

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:21.600
We feel great!

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:24.720
B-R-E-A-K-E-R-S!

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:28.470
Gooo Breakers!

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:44.770
Go, Breakers!

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:56.680
Granny. Thanks to you, and Mom, and Dad...

00:19:56.680 --> 00:20:05.390
I have so many friends. All of
those guys are my teammates.

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:23.560
Thank you. You all ended up supporting me.

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:26.390
Well, cheerleading's that sort of sport.

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:28.850
You've always said so yourself.

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:31.810
It's true.

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:33.890
You'll start coming to practice tomorrow, right?

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:36.470
We're a mess without our Captain.

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:39.100
That's right!

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:42.390
I will. I'll come.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:46.560
Performing with you guys
is why I do cheerleading now!

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.390
Whoa, it's the Winter Triangle.

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:58.350
Aren't you freezing?

00:20:58.350 --> 00:20:59.850
Haru.

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:03.560
Let's look at the stars for just a bit longer.

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:05.060
Fine.

00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:08.850
I'm going to beat this.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:13.770
Because all of you cheered me on.

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:15.600
I won't give up again.

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:24.770
Man, you're just too cool, Kazu. You've
overcome so many things all by yourself.

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:25.640
Haru...

00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:33.640
I'll never beat you in my lifetime. Even though
our coach wrote "Beat Kazu" in my notebook.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:35.310
Haru...

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:37.850
No, you'll beat me, Haru.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:39.020
What?

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:42.100
You'll definitely get a girlfriend first!

00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:43.890
N-No way!

00:21:43.890 --> 00:21:47.680
How have things been going
with Chihiro? I'm dying to know!

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:49.180
Nothing's happened!

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:51.270
Really?

00:21:54.850 --> 00:21:56.970
Thank you very much!

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:04.640
Domoto, what's up with you?

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:06.100
Nothing.

00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:10.560
The Breakers?! They're gonna compete
in the National Championship?

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:12.060
Seriously?

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:13.890
Then that means...

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:16.890
Sho Tokugawa will be there, too, right?!

00:22:18.930 --> 00:22:22.930
Tears of the Sun

00:22:32.890 --> 00:22:36.430
<i>Without even thinking, I shouted a reply</i>

00:22:36.430 --> 00:22:43.060
<i>The voice opening that new door</i>
<i>sounded like a tightly clenched fist</i>

00:22:43.060 --> 00:22:46.470
<i>Resounding with reassuring determination</i>

00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:49.850
<i>I think if I let out</i>
<i>(I've been waiting for this)</i>

00:22:49.850 --> 00:22:53.140
<i>All my pent-up energy</i>
<i>(I can change something)</i>

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:59.720
<i>We've always been looking for</i>
<i>something this cool! Ain't that right?</i>

00:22:59.720 --> 00:23:02.640
<i>Feeling insecure</i>
<i>(Oh my God!)</i>

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:05.930
<i>I fell into a funk</i>
<i>(Oh my pride!)</i>

00:23:05.930 --> 00:23:08.020
<i>Send that old me</i>
<i>(Don't give in!)</i>

00:23:08.020 --> 00:23:09.680
<i>A solid cheer</i>
<i>(Go, go!)</i>

00:23:09.680 --> 00:23:14.180
<i>Make encouraging motions</i>
<i>(Let's dance together!)</i>

00:23:14.180 --> 00:23:17.560
<i>Yes! Fly high, fly dive, up and away!</i>

00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:21.310
<i>Never hang your head and give up</i>
<i>(No!) </i>

00:23:21.310 --> 00:23:24.640
<i>Break up, break out, break it to smithereens</i>
<i>(Yes!)</i>

00:23:24.640 --> 00:23:27.930
<i>Smile together, break a sweat, show your guts!</i>
<i>(Guts!)</i>

00:23:27.930 --> 00:23:34.560
<i>Strike a victory pose toward the blue sky</i>
<i>(Jump! Jump! High V!)</i>

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:37.720
<i>Win over everybody's hearts!</i>

00:23:37.720 --> 00:23:41.100
<i>Go for that moment when</i>
<i>you meet a sparkling smile</i>

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:49.220
<i>Go, fight! Go, fight, win!</i>

00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:56.270
It's okay. Concentrate. You can
do it. Concentrate. Concentrate.

00:23:56.270 --> 00:23:58.220
--Concentrate. Concentrate. Concentrate. Con... Con...

00:23:58.220 --> 00:23:59.850
--What's wrong with Haru?
--Concentrate. Concentrate. Concentrate. Con... Con...

00:23:59.850 --> 00:24:01.100
--He's scaring me.
--Concentrate. Concentrate. Concentrate. Con... Con...

00:24:01.100 --> 00:24:03.520
--He's as fragile as a normal person.
--Concentrate. Concentrate. Concentrate. Con... Con...

00:24:03.520 --> 00:24:06.060
Con carne. Chili con carne. That sounds good.

00:24:06.060 --> 00:24:10.920
Next Episode: What I Wanted To Tell You

00:24:06.060 --> 00:24:09.390
Next Episode: What I Wanted To Tell You.

00:24:09.390 --> 00:24:10.930
Go! Fight! Win!
